./xmodel/sol-software2.log:2074:./RECON.md:51:- **Helali:** Zenodo **10.5281/zenodo.21479814** v1.0.1, pub. 2026-07-21 — "Exact Computer-Assisted Exclusion of the (72,108) Frontier in the Two-Dimensional Jacobian Problem" + GitHub `bilLkarkariy/jc2-72-108-exact-certificates` (1 star, 5 commits). Claim structure: transcribes BOTH residual systems of GGHV Prop 4.3; Case 2 killed by a unit-ideal identity 1 = ΣT_iR_i; Case 1 splits into s=±c branches, an identity forces h=0, unit-ideal certificates kill the h=0 specialization; an involution transports the hard certificate between sign branches. Hard certificate 89,105,967 bytes; multiplier ansatz a 2010×1925 rational linear system, fixed 1925×1925 minor with det 10 mod 71; independent gmpy2 replay of 13,410 number-field products, ~70 s on a laptop, marker `JC2_72_108_EXACT_REPLAY_PASS`. **Explicitly conditional** on correctness + faithful transcription of GGHV's reduction; explicitly "not a proof of JC(2)". AI disclosure: OpenAI Codex. No arXiv (no endorsement), no expert audit visible. [COMPETES-WITH-US — inspectable, plausible, unaudited]
