Reading of C9: the P-place value data fails the one-place PREcondition
(y has a zero, not a pole, at the place). On a one-place curve every
nonconstant polynomial has its unique pole at the place; y|_C is
nonconstant; so a curve owning a P-place as its ONLY place at infinity
would force y|_C = 0 — absurd. That one-line argument is the content
of C9a; C9b is its semigroup quantification: the only positive reading
of the exponent ladder sits strictly on the LOCAL side of the AM
dichotomy at every step, i.e. the P-places are finite-center-type
branches (y -> 0 along the place, toward the point [1:0:0]).

## 3. Adjudication

### 3.1 Fiber tier: outcomes (a) and (b) are structurally unreachable

The one-place hypothesis attaches to no pinned template object. The
fiber C is irreducible (f primitive, SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:29-30) with
>= 2 places forced by the template itself (P_1 != P_2, engine C10:
their series split at the characteristic level 32 since
a_1 - a_2 = 2 sqrt3 != 0), >= 4 places on the banked count
(SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:156), generically 2 + r_B + 42
(GROK-MONODROMY.md:149-174). So (AM-SG) simply does not constrain C,
and no violation of it can kill residue-A — outcome (a) is unreachable.
Equally, no "CONSISTENT with margins" report (b) is honest: the
inequality is not satisfied-with-slack, it is inapplicable, and its
reflected form is violated. The violation is REQUIRED structure: by
(AM-JAC) a Keller counterexample's f must not be one-place, and this
template complies at the strongest (semigroup-certified) level.

Deformation stability: the reflected-ladder margins are the exponent
gaps m_{i+1} - m_i, which are POSITIVE for every admissible genome
(edges have positive length; any Q-preserving deformation keeps
ascending characteristic levels, i.e. y bounded along every y-side
place — the root-chart convention itself, SHEET6-TEMPLATE.md:63-64).
Hence EVERY genome in this frame stays on the local side: the one-place
instrument cannot come alive at fiber tier for residue-A or for any of
its siblings (the @w4/@w3/@w2 book, SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:351-352) under
any deformation of the pinned data. This is a permanent wrong-object
theorem for the instrument, not a near-miss.

Margins, banked for the record (task request): the two AM-side defects
are exactly (20, 5) in 1/42 units — equal to the template's own edge
lengths (F_s -> G_m: n = 10 steps at 1/21 = 20; G_m -> P_i: n = 5 steps
at 1/42 = 5; SHEET6-TEMPLATE.md:115-123). The local-side slacks are the
same (+20, +5). The "5" is the tightest characteristic datum of the
genome (the +-w_i split sits only 5 levels below the cube split); any
future instrument that prices exponent gaps should start there. The
only banked tail-level pin (the no-log c_42 = 0 pin,
SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:711-772) sits at level 42 = 0 mod every d_i:
non-characteristic, no effect on the sequence — the characteristic data
is robust to every banked coefficient pin.

### 3.2 A(F) tier: NOT-DERIVABLE, and what would derive it

The binding object class is Jelonek's A(F): each component is a
one-place rational curve (J-1), so (AM-SG) PLUS rationality constrains
its delta-sequence — a genuine fresh kill test, pre-registered but not
run (SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:299-302). To run it one needs, per component:
its degree and the characteristic data at its unique place — i.e. the
CROSS-FIBER asymptotic-value correspondence a -> c_p(a) on the B-side
(components swept by (a, c_p(a))) and the x-side analogue, including
how the B-place partition varies and permutes over the a-line.

The template does not pin this, and the residual-32 variables DO NOT
supply it: all 84 unknowns of the banked decider
(SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:609-644: 42 high tails at levels >= 43, 26 low
tails, 6 dead-stretch coefficients, 3 Rabinowitsch inverses, 7 radical
generators) are y-side data of the SINGLE fiber f = a at the gauge
value. No variable carries a d/da datum. What would supply it, in
increasing cost: (i) differentiate the per-branch J1 transport
identities (SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:142-177) in the base direction to get
dc_p/da — cheapest, unexplored; (ii) the LR2 x-side build
(SHEET6-R1 sec 16.5; DIRECTIONB next-object 4), which prices the
x-side components (e' = 2 charge, GROK-MONODROMY.md:159-174); (iii) a
pencil-parameterized (a symbolic) rerun of the staged R1 build. Note
the ceiling is tight: sum of e_p-excess = 2g + 6 and per-value swallow
<= mu(F) = 6 (SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:278-297) already bound the component
degrees' Puiseux complexity — the A(F) delta-sequences will be SHORT,
so the AM chain there will be decisive once the degrees exist.

### 3.3 Relation to the banked AM record

The per-place arithmetic with actual kill power at fiber tier — the
valuation form (AM-2) of J(f,g) = 1 — is already exhausted: the
zero-slack identity ord_t f_y = -39 at the poles and the B-/x-window
